# Week 1–2: Project Understanding, Initialization and Database Design

## Objective

The objective of these two weeks was to understand the requirements of ThaparRent, establish the frontend and backend structure, and begin setting up the database for the campus rental marketplace.

## Work Completed

- Studied the requirements of a campus rental marketplace for TIET students.
- Initialized the frontend using React and Vite and the backend using Node.js and Express.
- Created the basic project structure, welcome page, and backend health-check endpoint.
- Started configuring PostgreSQL and Prisma ORM for database management.
- Designed the initial User and Listing models to represent students and rental items.

## Challenges / Observations

An important challenge was organizing the frontend, backend, and database components into a structured application. Understanding how Prisma connects the backend with PostgreSQL was also an important part of the initial development process.

## Learning

Learned the basic roles of React, Vite, Node.js, Express, PostgreSQL, and Prisma in full-stack development. Also understood how database models represent users and rental listings.

## Week 1–2 Outcome

The initial project structure was established, and the foundation for database integration was planned and developed. These steps prepared the project for implementing rental listing management and student authentication in the upcoming weeks.
